// TEST: OrbIdx Wreath Annotated Read (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4003
// WRITING the class down stays refused even though READING one is now
// implemented -- and this probe exists because the read path is exactly the
// argument that used to be given for opening the annotation. It is not enough
// on its own.
//
// The two powers differ in what they admit. DEDUCTION reaches a wreath class
// only through the one shape that has a traversal nest (a comm tie over a
// repeated compact argument, `IR.deduceWreathTie`), so every wreath value in
// existence was FILLED by that nest. An ANNOTATION names the class in the
// abstract and admits bindings no producer can fill -- the binding below wants
// a 21-cell pool out of `zero`, and there is no writer for it. A readable
// object that cannot be written is not progress; the missing half is now the
// WRITE side, which is what the refusal text says.
//
// 193 pins the same door with a named type alias; this one pins it INLINE and
// then subscripts the binding, so the refusal has to come from the annotation
// rather than from the read (which would now succeed).
let R: Array<Float64 like OrbIdx<[(2,+), (2,+)], 3>> = zero |> compute
let cell = R(0, 1, 0, 1)
// EXPECT: typecheck failure — a written (annotated) OrbIdx class has no producer.
